window.products.push({"id":245356,"name":"AlmaCura Palo Santo Sticks 1lb Bulk Wholesale High Resine Organic Certified from Peru (NOT Ecuador). Ethically Sustainably Harvested. Protection, Medi","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":36.55,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81OL8GtPBSL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","description":"PALO SANTO is a tree, the wood of which is of spiritual significance to indigenous people in South America. The wood is considered sacred, and its Spanish meaning is “holy wood”. PALO SANTO is a sacred tree which grows in select parts of South America. It has been used for centuries by shamans in ritual prayer, ceremonies and healing. Rich in brain-oxygenating terpenes such as limonene and a-terpineol, PALO SANTO has an uplifting and positive effect. ETHICALLY HARVESTED - Almacura Palo Santo sticks are ethically and sustainably harvested respecting the environment and the sacredness of the tree. The wood is selected only from the highest quality trees ensuring that you receive the most potent and aromatic sticks. HOW TO USE IT: Take one stick at 45° and light it with a candle, match or lighter. Allow the Palo Santo stick to burn for 30 seconds to a minute, then carefully blow it out. Allow the stick to smolder and release its scent, adding a pleasant and natural fragrance to any room in your home or office. The smoke released is believed to have purifying properties, it is often used to cleanse the energy of a space or a person before meditation or a spiritual practice. Never leave the burning PALO SANTO unattended. Re-light the stick as many times as you need. CONNECTION: Our palo santo sticks are not just a product, they are a connection to ancient spiritual practices and beliefs. They are a way to honor the sacredness of the palo santo tree and to connect with the energy of the earth. When you use these sticks, you are participating in a centuries-old tradition and connecting with something much greater than ouselves. CERTIFIED: The demand of palo santo is quite high throughout the world. Due to this, there are some concerns that the tree may be being harvested beyond it’s capacity. Following very strict rules about PALO SANTO harvesting, our company endorses the environmental protection obtaining the PALO SANTO harvsting certificate extended by the Peruvian Forestal Administration.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/81OL8GtPBSL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"AlmaCura","source_asin":"B0C1W3MV8V","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-245356","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0C1W3MV8V","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B0C1W3MV8V","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
